[2026-09-29 16:30] Linux validation run, planned and timed. NOT YET RUN. This is what closes the two unmet Gate 1 items.
why: Kept here so it survives the conversation. WHY Linux: not the shell - macOS File.Sync is F_FULLFSYNC (flushes the drive's own cache), Linux fsync usually returns once data reaches the drive, so fsync-bound numbers differ by an order of magnitude and the PRD targets are Linux targets; SO_REUSEPORT UDP and the /proc/net/snmp drop counter are Linux-only.
Needs a Linux KERNEL, not necessarily a bare-metal box: cloud VM (timings noisy on shared disks), dedicated VM, or Docker-on-Mac (fine for crash suite and SO_REUSEPORT, NOT for throughput).
Setup: build-essential jq netcat-openbsd curl git (cgo for -race); Go 1.22+; repo on ext4/xfs, NOT tmpfs or a bind mount; sysctl net.core.rmem_max=26214400 rmem_default=8388608; ulimit -n 65535.
Run, in order: (1) make check; make crash; the crash suite under -race; make fuzz. (2) make build; ingestd with the dev config; scripts/send_samples.sh must print "all checks passed"; ingest_udp_kernel_drops should be a number, not NaN. (3) record `uname -a; lscpu; free -h; df -T .; lsblk -d -o NAME,ROTA,MODEL,SIZE; go version` then make bench. Quote ONLY durable_ack=1 results as headline. Targets: PutBatch/always/producers=16 >= 50k records/s; PutLatency/always p99 <= 10ms; PutBatch/interval >= 200k records/s; Seal/records=100000 <= 100ms. (4) RSS at 100k records/s, target < 300 MiB: needs a load generator, which the repo does NOT have (cmd/bench is Packaging's); measure with `/usr/bin/time -v` or VmHWM from /proc/<pid>/status.
Time: ~30-45 min total, ~15 of compute. Measured on the Mac: make check 61s, crash 25s per variant, crash under -race 44s, send_samples ~10s. ESTIMATED, not timed: setup 5-10 min, make bench 5-10 min (~30 benchmarks at ~1s each plus 200k-record and 100k-record fixtures), RSS ~10 min with a sender or +15 to write one.
Return: bench-env.txt, bench-results.txt, tails of make check and make crash. A make crash FAILURE on Linux would be a real finding - rename and directory-fsync semantics differ from APFS - so save its full output.
affects: Gate 1 (recorded benchmarks, RSS), benchmarks/results/ (Packaging's directory)

