[2026-09-29 21:00] B5 started: intel/ulpf_intel/fingerprint.py (structural fingerprint, Drain3 template set, drift score). 47 pytest pass.
why: fortinet.log vs a fresh half of itself scores 0.0 (bar: < 0.1). fortinet vs fortinet_drift.log scores 0.5405 on structure alone and 0.6345 with the drifted file's real quarantine rate (0.94); the PRD bar is >= 0.6, which holds ONLY with the quarantine term, and the test says so instead of hiding it (structure alone must stay in [0.35, 0.6), i.e. above the alert threshold). Signals name srcip->src, dstip->dst, srcport->sport, dstport->dport and the epoch timestamp change. First version paired spurious renames (policytype->dstcountry) because a lone same-shape candidate was accepted regardless of name; now requires name similarity >= 0.5. Also collapsed the 15 identical "qstr->word" shape signals into one "quoting changed". Found by looking at the output, not by a test. Mutation-checked: rename threshold 0 and keyset term zeroed each fail a test.
Weights are PRD defaults (0.30/0.25/0.20/0.15/0.10), not yet tuned. drain3 0.9.1 imports cachetools without declaring it; pinned explicitly in pyproject.
